From a219c0c52caec12393afffa9b75c77ac878e5458 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:33:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): upstream-sync REFUSED names failing jobs/tests and
 main-baseline vs candidate-only [daveey]

A red full suite printed only "REFUSED: the full suite failed on <sha>: <run>": no job, no
test, and nothing saying whether main already failed the same tests, so a pre-existing main e2e
failure read as upstream's fault (5 whys on t_01a18f436c8ec2ae: Candidate dropped the run id,
so nothing could read its jobs; PR380 deferred the diagnostic).

New scripts/ci/upstream_sync_diagnostics.py prints under the REFUSED line: each failed required
job with its URL and parsed failing test ids (nightly_e2e.failing_tests), then compares them with
main at the sync's fork point (merge-base) using only runs that tested exactly that sha: ci.yaml
on main (push/dispatch), and nightly-e2e runs whose "Resolve ref" log names that sha (a nightly's
head_sha is the workflow commit, not the tested one). Ids main also fails are a main-baseline
failure ("not evidence that upstream caused them"); ids a complete passing/failing baseline run
did not fail are "candidate-only failure observed ... not proof of upstream causation"; anything
else is "baseline comparison unknown". The e2e set links an open nightly-e2e card only with
nightly-e2e provenance and the exact failure_key fingerprint; an unreadable board/state says
"lookup unavailable", never "no owner".

The gate is unchanged: the verdict is decided before diagnostics run and any diagnostic fault
prints "diagnostics unavailable" with REFUSED kept (tested). Candidate gains run_id.
